  "title": "Capacitor, radial electrolytic",
  "summary": "Polarized aluminum electrolytic can, 6.3 mm across, with two leads on 2.5 mm. The longer lead is `pos`, and the stripe on the sleeve marks `neg`. Wire `pos` to the higher voltage. A reverse voltage past 1 V warns. Set its capacitance. It starts where the circuit's DC solution puts it, which on a pin that is still an input is not 0 V. Set `initial`, such as \"0\", to start it at that voltage.",
